cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework for describing how a
  shared multidimensional real-resource world K, actor-relative access and
  usability views K_i derived from that shared world, and actor-specific
  subjective evaluation and expectation states P_i condition actor-side
  processes and events A_i. Delta K(S, tau) denotes realized real-resource
  change under an observation and accounting specification S and interval tau,
  where S includes resource coordinates, accounting boundary, and transformation
  convention. Delta K is treated as an S-indexed change schema rather than a
  single universal mathematical value type; conceptually, Delta K(S, tau) may
  take values in a scope-specific domain D_S. E_i[Delta K(S, tau)] denotes an
  actor-specific expected realized resource change where an expectation is
  defined. Planned or chosen resource changes are projection-specific and are
  not identified with this forecast. Preferences, desirability, credit
  assessments, beliefs, and related structures remain in P_i rather than being
  identified with the expectation itself. VFT does not fix a universal
  probability measure, expectation-formation equation, action-selection rule,
  market-equilibrium condition, or aggregation law. Economic equilibrium,
  budget constraints, accounting identities, surplus, decentralized adjustment,
  micro-macro accounting or observation linkages, and reputation- or
  credit-economy models are treated as domain-specific projection candidates
  requiring additional economic and measurement assumptions.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
keywords:
  - value-field theory
